{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/122680","id":4328313593,"node_id":"PR_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABAfzS-Q","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/122680","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/122680.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/122680.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/122680","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/122680/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/122680/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/122680/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/statuses/5d63a641c79b5fb83e8d6752864c739f3254d720","number":122680,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"Fix AreaLight3D energy in SDFGI when physical light units enable","user":{"login":"cosformula","id":18232501,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4MjMyNTAx","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/18232501?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/cosformula","html_url":"https://github.com/cosformula","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cosformula/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cosformula/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cosformula/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cosformula/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cosformula/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cosformula/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cosformula/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cosformula/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cosformula/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"## What problem(s) does this PR solve?\r\n\r\n- Closes #122457.\r\n- AreaLight3D energy was not converted from luminous power to luminous intensity in SDFGI when physical light units were enabled, making indirect lighting `2 * PI` too bright.\r\n\r\n## Additional information\r\n\r\nApply the same `1 / (2 * PI)` conversion already used by direct lighting and VoxelGI to both dynamic and static SDFGI light packing paths.\r\n\r\nThis conversion appears to have been missed when AreaLight3D support was added in #108219. That change added area-light packing to both SDFGI paths, while the equivalent VoxelGI path received the correct `1 / (2 * PI)` conversion.\r\n\r\n### Before the fix\r\n<img width=\"1280\" height=\"720\" alt=\"before-on\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/543a24dd-cb8b-484b-bdac-884e7d408cef\" />\r\n\r\n### After the fix\r\n<img width=\"1280\" height=\"720\" alt=\"after-on\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/50f02453-c44c-4175-b2ed-22571598515e\" />\r\n\r\n\r\n## AI disclosure\r\n\r\nI used AI to help confirm and understand the root cause of this issue, and to review the proposed fix. I reproduced the issue and verified the fix myself.\r\n","labels":[{"id":73330064,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw3MzMzMDA2NA==","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/bug","name":"bug","description":"","color":"ff6055","default":true,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":279096997,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNzkwOTY5OTc=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/archived","name":"archived","description":"","color":"aaaaaa","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":279098111,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNzkwOTgxMTE=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:rendering","name":"topic:rendering","description":"","color":"ffee88","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":2666708289,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNjY2NzA4Mjg5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:3d","name":